# Tooling state
.remember/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/

# Polly-generated welcome clip — regenerated by setup-agentcore.py on every deploy.
agent/welcome-zh.mp3

# Amazon DCV Web Client SDK (EULA-licensed, not redistributable) — fetched by
# scripts/01-install-deps.sh from public AWS CloudFront on every deploy.
chatbot/public/dcvjs/

# Latency testing sandbox — independent clone + ap-northeast-1 deployment
test-deployments/

# Local e2e harness — needs a live deployment, so it stays out of git.
e2e-a2a/
.pytest_cache/
admin-console/scripts/
.playwright-mcp/

docs/superpowers/

# Build outputs: the shared device catalog is copied into each IoT Lambda by
# scripts/01-install-deps.sh, since CDK only packages a Lambda's own directory.
# Source of truth is shared/device-catalog.json.
cdk/lambda/*/device-catalog.json
cdk/lambda/*/device_catalog.py
# Same arrangement for the Agent Registry helper.
# Source of truth is shared/agent_registry.py.
cdk/lambda/*/agent_registry.py
# And for the A2A grant policy, which the admin API (per-user memberships and the
# revocation sweep) and the pre-token trigger (global grants injected into the
# claim) must both apply IDENTICALLY. Source of truth is shared/subagent_policy.py.
cdk/lambda/*/subagent_policy.py
# And for the authorizer-conformance rule, shared by the admin API's check route and
# the contract generator. Source of truth is shared/a2a_conformance.py.
cdk/lambda/*/a2a_conformance.py
# And for the platform manifest we publish to third-party A2A agent teams, plus the
# session-propagation module it reads the metadata key from. The manifest is GENERATED
# from the modules that enforce each rule, so a stale copy would have us publishing a
# contract we no longer honour. Source of truth is shared/a2a_manifest.py.
cdk/lambda/*/a2a_manifest.py
cdk/lambda/*/a2a_session.py
# And for the scenario model plus the solar maths and the shared schedule payload,
# which the scenario runner and the admin API both need. Source of truth is
# shared/.
cdk/lambda/*/scenarios.py
cdk/lambda/*/solar.py
cdk/lambda/*/scenario_schedules_shared.py
cdk/lambda/*/user_settings.py
# The Memory actor-id rule also reaches the admin API, which reads a user's
# short-term transcript back for the chatbot's login history and therefore has
# to name the actor the exact same way the agent wrote it under. Source of truth
# is shared/memory_actor.py.
cdk/lambda/*/memory_actor.py
# And for the Memory actor-id rule, which the orchestrator's container needs a
# copy of because it is built from agent/ alone while the A2A sub-agents get all
# of shared/. Source of truth is shared/memory_actor.py.
agent/memory_actor.py
# Same for the device brief the orchestrator attaches to each delegation, and the
# catalog it is generated from. Source of truth is shared/.
agent/device_brief.py
agent/device_catalog.py
agent/device-catalog.json
# The prompt-example library, copied into the chatbot's bundle. The chatbot and
# scripts/sim/personas.py read the SAME file so "what this system can do" is
# stated once; a second copy would drift, and the symptom is discovering
# mid-demo that nothing exercises some agent. Source of truth is
# shared/prompt-examples.json.
chatbot/src/generated/

# Latency/cost measurement runs (scripts/measure-baseline.py and the ab-* probes).
# Development-phase output: a baseline is only comparable against another baseline
# from the SAME deployment, so an archive from one account is noise to anyone else.
# The conclusions that mattered are inlined in docs/agent-design-principles*.md and
# docs/architecture-and-design.md instead, so they survive without the raw runs.
docs/measurements/
